-- A mismatch between types one of which is cyclic is the cycle's
-- INFINITE TYPE, never a TYPE MISMATCH printing the cycle. `( x, x )` makes
-- `x`'s type `a = ( a, a )` (unification does not occurs-check a binding;
-- the boundary does, checker-v2.md §8.2), and the record then fails against
-- it. That failure must not be a TYPE MISMATCH printing the record's `zb`
-- as a tuple unrolled until the printer's node budget runs out (37 KB) and
-- the list's other elements as `…`. Expected: one INFINITE TYPE, written
-- down with `a` standing for the repeat.
f x = [ x, ( x, x ), { zb = x, za = "s" } ]
